<!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
<h1>1. Executive Summary</h1>
<p>
Modern machine learning models increasingly automate high-stakes decisions across hiring, consumer lending, healthcare prioritization, and insurance pricing. While these automated decision systems promise efficiency, they silently scale and automate historical societal discrimination embedded in training datasets.
</p>
<p>
<strong>FairSight</strong> is an end-to-end, production-ready <strong>AI Bias Compliance and Mitigation Platform</strong> created by team <strong>Robo maters</strong> for the <strong>GDSC Solution Challenge 2026</strong>. Siting between trained machine learning models and end users, FairSight functions as an intelligent firewall: detecting algorithmic disparities, synthesizing root causes through <strong>Google Gemini 2.0 Flash</strong> multi-LLM consensus, mathematically repairing datasets via the Kamiran & Calders reweighing algorithm, and intercepting discriminatory inferences before real people are harmed.
</p>

<!-- SECTION 2: PROBLEM STATEMENT -->
<h1>2. Problem Statement: Algorithmic Discrimination</h1>

<h2>2.1 The Silent Scaling of Algorithmic Discrimination</h2>
<p>
Unlike human decision-makers whose biases are bounded by individual capacity, biased algorithms scale discrimination across thousands or millions of users per minute:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Employment Screening:</strong> Automated resume filters trained on historical technical hires systematically penalize female candidates and minority applicants.</li>
  <li><strong>Credit & Lending:</strong> Underwriting algorithms produce lower loan approval rates and higher interest rates for minority applicants due to historical redlining and credit wealth gaps.</li>
  <li><strong>Healthcare Prioritization:</strong> Clinical triage systems allocate lower priority and funding to minority patients with the same illness severity as majority patients.</li>
  <li><strong>Criminal Justice:</strong> Recidivism scoring algorithms yield false-positive risk scores for minority defendants at nearly double the rate of majority defendants.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2.2 The "Fairness Through Blindness" Fallacy & Proxy Leakage</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>The Blindness Fallacy:</strong> Merely dropping protected attributes (race, gender, age) from a model does NOT prevent discrimination. High-dimensional models easily reconstruct protected characteristics through correlational proxies.
</div>
<ul>
  <li><strong>ZIP Code / Location:</strong> Acts as a direct proxy for race and socioeconomic status due to residential segregation.</li>
  <li><strong>Alma Mater & Sports:</strong> Act as proxies for gender and class.</li>
  <li><strong>Employment Gaps:</strong> Correlate strongly with pregnancy, maternity leave, and caregiving duties.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2.3 Global Regulatory Compliance Pressures</h2>
<table class="data-table">
  <tr>
    <th>Regulation / Legal Standard</th>
    <th>Jurisdiction</th>
    <th>Legal Scope & Statutory Penalties</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>EU AI Act (Regulation 2024/1689)</strong></td>
    <td>European Union</td>
    <td>Mandatory bias audits, data governance, and risk mitigation for High-Risk AI systems. Fines reach up to <strong>&euro;35,000,000 or 7% of total global annual turnover</strong>.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>US EEOC Uniform Guidelines (80% Rule)</strong></td>
    <td>United States</td>
    <td>Title VII enforcement: Selection rate for any race, sex, or ethnic group less than 4/5ths (80%) of the top group constitutes evidence of adverse impact.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>NYC Local Law 144</strong></td>
    <td>New York City, USA</td>
    <td>Mandates annual independent algorithmic bias audits for automated employment decision tools (AEDTs) before use.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>GDPR Article 22</strong></td>
    <td>European Union</td>
    <td>Protects individuals from solely automated decisions carrying legal effects and grants the right to human intervention.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<!-- SECTION 3: THE FAIRSIGHT SOLUTION -->
<h1>3. The FairSight Solution</h1>

<p>
FairSight shifts algorithmic fairness from a retrospective, once-a-year audit into an <strong>active, continuous runtime compliance firewall</strong>.
</p>

<h2>3.1 How FairSight Works in Production</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Ingest & Verify:</strong> Users upload datasets or stream inference payloads. Datasets are parsed in-memory, hashed via SHA-256 for cryptographic provenance, and scanned for PII.</li>
  <li><strong>Calculate Disparity:</strong> The statistical engine computes Demographic Parity, Equalized Odds, Disparate Impact, and Intersectional Radar metrics.</li>
  <li><strong>Multi-LLM Consensus Reasoning:</strong> Google Gemini 2.0 Flash coordinates with secondary LLMs to produce plain-English diagnostic narratives without hallucinations.</li>
  <li><strong>Real-Time Interception (Firewall):</strong> Live inferences are counterfactually tested. If flipping a protected attribute changes the decision, the prediction is quarantined and routed to human review.</li>
  <li><strong>Magic Debiasing:</strong> Reweighs training distributions mathematically (Kamiran & Calders) to generate a balanced, retraining-ready dataset.</li>
  <li><strong>Certify:</strong> Generates regulator-ready PDF audit reports aligned with the EU AI Act and EEOC.</li>
</ol>

