<!-- SECTION 6: MATHEMATICAL FORMULATIONS -->
<h1>6. Mathematical Approach & Formulations</h1>

<h3>6.1 Demographic Parity Difference (DPD)</h3>
<div class="formula-box">
  DPD = | P(Y_hat = 1 | A = 0) - P(Y_hat = 1 | A = 1) | &le; 0.10
</div>
<p>Ensures that the rate of positive outcomes is statistically independent of demographic group membership.</p>

<h3>6.2 Disparate Impact Ratio (DIR) / Four-Fifths Rule</h3>
<div class="formula-box">
  DIR = P(Y_hat = 1 | A = 0) / P(Y_hat = 1 | A = 1) &ge; 0.80
</div>
<p>Directly measures compliance with the US EEOC 80% Rule under Title VII.</p>

<h3>6.3 Equalized Odds Difference (EOD)</h3>
<div class="formula-box">
  EOD = max( |TPR_unprivileged - TPR_privileged|, |FPR_unprivileged - FPR_privileged| ) &le; 0.10
</div>
<p>Constrains both True Positive Rates and False Positive Rates to ensure equal predictive accuracy across groups.</p>

<h3>6.4 Kamiran & Calders Reweighing Weight</h3>
<div class="formula-box">
  W(s, y) = [ P(S = s) &times; P(Y = y) ] / P(S = s &and; Y = y)
</div>
<p>Assigns sample weights during training such that the weighted demographic parity difference equals zero.</p>

